人那了。”“小心。”钟氏定定的望着柳蓉。柳蓉微微一笑，重重的点了点头才转身离开。梨园二奶奶的产房中传来撕心裂肺的喊声，继而不知是谁打翻了东西，竟传出清脆的声音，刺的人心不安。门外等待的二爷面色一紧，快步走近产房，便见李妈妈满脸苍白，慌慌张张的走出。“怎么了？”“二奶奶，二奶奶的羊水破了……”“那孩子呢？”“孩子……孩子没有出来……”“那还傻站着做什么，还不快去请大夫！”柳蓉离开住所，便快步向主院走去，毕竟之前耽误了一些时间，柳蓉却是不敢在路上再浪费时间，古代的封建家庭可和现代祖辈对小辈满心的关怀，犯一点错，也模糊过不同。在这里，最容不得的，便是小辈犯错，不，或许应该说容不得庶女犯错。穿过长长的走廊，又绕过梅园假山，走了大约一盏茶的时间才到得太夫人住的院子，大量的运动，让柳蓉冷静下来，就是这冰天雪地的寒冷也淡了一些。太夫人的院子外，几个丫鬟婆子远远的来回搓着手，跺着脚走动，围着主庭院外面，却没有靠近屋子，显是被主人们打发出来的。巧儿便在其中，只是此时的巧儿却和在她母亲房中不同，却是满脸讨好的笑容对着一位装束严谨的中年婆子。柳蓉挑了挑眉，脚下却是放下速度，不慌不忙的向太夫人的屋子走去。那中年婆子却是眼尖，一眼便看到她出现，没有继续和巧儿寒暄，却是快步迎上前：“可是蓉姐儿？我是太夫人身边伺候的陈妈妈。”柳蓉点了点头，这太夫人还真如钟氏说的对她漠不关心，竟是连身边的人都对她印象不深，还要问上一句方能确认。见柳蓉点头，陈妈妈快速开口：“赶紧进去吧，太夫人来来回回都问起你三次了。”柳蓉对着陈妈妈再次点头，才随着陈妈妈走进屋子，屋门打开，屋中竟坐了三个人。除却端坐的人外，便见最中央那看起来慈祥万分的老人家身后还站着一个一身粉色小袄，头上簪着蝴蝶赤金步摇，看起来俏皮可爱的少女。只是这少女看到她似乎有些紧张，拽着老妇人那一身墨绿色绣祥云的衣衫衣角撒娇的手不觉的露出一丝青筋，但即便如此，柳蓉还是注意到对方在见到自己的瞬间，眼底迸发出的，那掩饰不住的兴奋。柳蓉不动声色扫了一眼其他人，便见太夫人左侧坐着一个三十来岁的妇人，面上表情严肃，毫无喜意。而太夫人的右侧却是坐着一个一身橘色绣水墨图的少妇，对着太夫人时一脸笑意，见到自己时神色却自然而然冷淡三分。柳蓉默默将众人的表情记在心中，才对着中央看起来万分慈祥的太夫人请安：“柳蓉见过太夫人。”柳蓉的话一落，便感觉到屋子里瞬间一静，连呼吸声都小了许多。好一会，才听一个尖锐的声音响起：“蓉姐儿，你入屋不同母亲祖母请安便也罢了，怎么？连太祖母都忘了怎么喊了吗？钟姨娘是怎么教导的，当初就不该答应大爷，让钟姨娘照养你。”说话之人正是太夫人右侧一身橘色袄子的妇人，只见她面色冰冷，眼底毫不掩饰的流露出一丝厌恶。柳蓉眉头微微一皱，看来这位就是那个一直只闻其名却不曾见过的刘姨娘，不，现在应该唤做刘大奶奶。“你这是做什么。会吓坏孩子的。”慈祥温和的声音响起：“快到太祖奶奶身边来，怎么能太称祖奶奶太夫人呢，这般见外，可不是我们柳家人的风格啊。”随着这声音，柳蓉便见一双有些皱，却看起来光滑十分的手伸到自己身前。“是。”柳蓉顺势乖巧的走到太夫人身边，眼角余光忍不住扫向太夫人，便见太夫人用一种很是奇特的眼神看着她，看到最后竟是露出满意的笑容。“大奶奶果然没骗我，蓉姐儿这小模样确实和九姑娘有些相像，就是可惜瘦弱了些，若是神情再有几分相似，便更加不错了。”见太夫人一直不断的打量自己，又说出这样的话，柳蓉眉头不禁紧紧皱起。“杜鹃，去，取一些首饰出来，这蓉姐儿打扮也太过素气了，这样子若是入了宫选秀，还不得让宫里的嬷嬷觉着我们侯府没照料好这孩子。”柳蓉猛的抬头，望了一眼太夫人身后露出笑容的少女，又望了一眼太夫人，再看大夫人阴沉的面目和大奶奶噙着一丝冷笑的嘴角。“太祖奶奶，您怕是记错了，入宫选秀的秀女是九姑姑，不是蓉儿。”柳蓉快速的开口道，随即又低下头，手指不安的卷动衣角，看起来怯怯的。只是低下的脸上却没有那股子局促，一双杏眼不断的转动，入宫选秀这是皇恩，若是选中了，在古代人心中自然是飞黄腾达的机会，可这些人却是将这样的机会拱手让给她这个府中最不得重视的人，不用想，其中肯定有猫腻，这件事情绝不能答应！太夫人眉头收紧，似乎没料到柳蓉会这般开口。大夫人更是微微讶异的看向柳蓉，大奶奶却是看着柳蓉眼底一丝狠毒闪过。柳蓉满是不安的站着，仿佛怕旁人不信一般，怯怯的再次开口道：“我真的听府中的人说过，要入宫选秀的是九姑姑，大家都说凭着九姑姑的品相，绝对是有可能成妃子的人物。”“你定是听错了，这选秀之事原本就定下，是由你入宫选秀，只是那时候你身体不好，所以才没同你说。只是现在选秀的日子近了，才不得不告诉你。”站在太夫人身后的少女急忙开口道。“九姑娘说的是，不过要入宫，也不能这个样子入宫，这般怯弱，凭的失了侯府的气度，正好府里请了教养嬷嬷，你入宫前便跟着教养嬷嬷生活一段时间吧。”太夫人摁了摁少女的手，对着柳蓉仿佛施舍一般说道。柳蓉将这一切看在眼中，心中忍不住冒起怒气，她不知道这入宫选秀，为何九姑娘如此避之不及，可己所不欲勿施于人，这帮人竟要这样硬生生的将自己躲避的事情就此安在她身上，都是侯府的女儿，却如此对她，这是何等过分！柳蓉抬头站起：“太夫人说的是，我这般模样会失了侯府的气度，只是不知道欺君之罪，会给侯府带来怎样的麻烦？”刘大奶奶眉头一皱：“你在说什么呢，难得祖母开恩，还让你跟着教养嬷嬷学习，你怎可如此说话！”一旁的大夫人抬头看向柳蓉，当看到柳蓉昂首挺胸再不是之前怯弱的模样时，眼中精光一闪，却是露出一丝笑意。“太祖母让我跟着教养嬷嬷学习，我自是感激，只是有些人不知道说了什么，要让太祖母晚节不保，做出有害侯府之事，我却是不能答应。”柳蓉看着刘大奶奶，声音铿锵有力。有些时候，装傻充愣既然不行，那就只能奋起直冲！而现在面对刘大奶奶一行人，正是这样的时候。“娘，蓉姐儿说的话不无道理，您不能再这么惯着璇儿了。”温和端庄的声音不紧不慢的响起，柳蓉忍不住看向声源，便见大夫人对着她笑着点了点头。听到大夫人的话，九姑娘赶忙看向太夫人：“奶奶，璇儿不要入宫，璇儿死也不要入宫，如今圣上都已经年过半百，听说身体还很是不好，恐怕……恐怕……”“闭嘴！当今圣上的事情也是你可以随便议论的吗？都是我平时将你宠坏了。”太夫人眉头一蹙，打断九姑娘的话。“奶奶！璇儿的性子若是入宫，定会被吃的骨头都不剩的！”柳璇赶忙改了口，拽住太夫人的衣角，可怜兮兮的望着太夫人。太夫人看着柳璇心疼的眉头都皱起：“宫中虽然要求侯府出女儿入宫，却不曾点名，我看，蓉姐儿这性子就不错，入宫说不定还能帮侯府更进一步。”", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/houmenyinu/3.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Chapter 3 Liu Rong's heart warmed because of her partiality, but she stepped forward to hold down Mrs. Zhong and stop her from getting up: \"Mother, you are overthinking. No matter what, I am also the great-great-granddaughter of the Dowager Madam, and I represent the face of the Liu family. Not to mention other things, it is for the other girls in the Liu family who want to leave the palace. They cannot marry me casually. But you can't panic yourself just because of a few words from a maid who can't stand the stage.\" Mrs. Zhong held the coat in her hand. Slightly loose, but still holding on, Liu Rong looked carefully and showed a slightly naughty smile to Mrs. Zhong: \"Not to mention this, just because your daughter survived the disaster and became smart, whatever happened is not solved easily. Ronger is now, not afraid of something happening, just afraid that something will not happen, so you can rest assured!\" After saying that, Liu Rong reached out to take the clothes in Mrs. Zhong's hand without waiting for Mrs. Zhong to speak, and hung them aside again. Although Mrs. Zhong would accompany her to see Madam Tai, she would feel more at ease, but since Mrs. Tai had carried Aunt Liu, she would definitely not want to see Mrs. Zhong. This would make Mrs. Zhong go to Madam Tai for her sake, and I am afraid that she would not be able to help her, but would also injure Mrs. Zhong. \"You are so clever.\" Mrs. Zhong couldn't help but poked Liu Rong's forehead with her finger, but there was a smile on her face, and she seemed to be a little disappointed: \"You have grown up.\" \"That's what my mother taught me!\" Liu Rong said with a smile before standing up: \"Mother, I will go to the madam first.\" \"Be careful.\" Mrs. Zhong looked at Liu Rong steadily. Liu Rong smiled slightly and nodded heavily before turning and leaving. Heartbreaking shouts came from the delivery room of the second mistress of Liyuan, and then a clear sound came from someone who had knocked something over, which made people uneasy. The second master who was waiting outside the door looked tense and quickly approached the delivery room. He saw Mother Li walking out in a panic with her face pale. \"What's wrong?\" \"Second Grandma, Second Grandma's amniotic water broke...\" \"Where's the child?\" \"The child... the child didn't come out...\" \"Then what are you doing standing there stupidly? Why don't you go call a doctor!\" Liu Rong left the residence and walked quickly to the main courtyard. After all, she had wasted some time before, but Liu Rong did not dare to waste any more time on the road. The feudal family in ancient times is different from the modern ancestors who are full of care for their younger generations, making even the slightest mistake. Here, the most unacceptable thing is for juniors to make mistakes. No, perhaps it should be said that it is not allowed for concubines to make mistakes. After walking through the long corridor and around the rockery in the plum garden, it took about a cup of tea to arrive at the courtyard where the Dowager lived. A lot of exercise helped Liu Rong calm down, and even the coldness in the ice and snow became less intense. Outside the Madam's courtyard, several maids and women were rubbing their hands back and forth from a distance, stomping around, surrounding the main courtyard, but not approaching the house. It was obvious that they had been sent away by their masters. Qiao'er was among them, but Qiao'er at this time was different from the one in her mother's room. Instead, she was facing a middle-aged woman in strict attire with a fawning smile on her face. Liu Rong raised her eyebrows, but she slowed down and walked towards the Madam's house calmly. The middle-aged woman was sharp-eyed and saw her appear at a glance. She did not continue to greet Qiao'er, but hurried forward to greet her: \"But Sister Rong? I am Mother Chen who serves the wife.\" Liu Rong nodded. The wife was really indifferent to her as Zhong said. In fact, even the people around her were not impressed by her, and she had to ask a question to confirm. Seeing Liu Rong nodding, Mother Chen quickly said: \"Hurry in, Mrs. Tai has asked about you three times.\" Liu Rong nodded again to Mother Chen, and then followed Mother Chen into the house. The door opened, and there were three people sitting in the room. In addition to the people sitting upright, behind the kind-looking old man in the center stood a cute and cute girl wearing a pink coat and a red gold butterfly hairpin on her head. It was just that the girl seemed a little nervous when she saw her, and her coquettish hand holding the corner of the old woman's dark green dress embroidered with auspicious clouds revealed a trace of veins. But even so, Liu Rong still noticed the unconcealable excitement that burst out from the other person's eyes the moment she saw her. Liu Rong glanced at the others calmly and saw a woman in her thirties sitting on the left side of the concubine, with a serious expression on her face and no joy at all. On the right side of the wife, there was a young woman wearing orange embroidery with ink drawings. She smiled when she looked at the wife, but when she saw herself, her expression was naturally cold. Liu Rong silently remembered everyone's expressions in her heart, and then greeted the Madam in the center who looked extremely kind: \"Liu Rong has met the Madam.\" As soon as Liu Rong finished speaking, she felt that the room was silent for a moment, and even her breathing became much quieter. After a while, I heard a sharp voice: \"Sister Rong, you don't have to greet your mother and grandmother when you enter the house. What? Have you even forgotten how to call your great-grandmother? How did Aunt Zhong teach you that you should not have promised to let Aunt Zhong take care of you in the first place.\" The person who spoke was the woman in an orange coat on the right side of the concubine. Her face was cold, and there was an undisguised trace of disgust in her eyes. Liu Rong frowned slightly. It seemed that this was the Aunt Liu whom she had only heard of by name but never met. No, she should be called Grandma Liu now. \"What are you doing? It will scare the child.\" A kind and gentle voice sounded: \"Come to Grandma Taizu, how can you call Grandma Grandma and Mrs. Taizu too much? This is not the style of our Liu family.\" Following this voice, Liu Rong saw a pair of wrinkled but smooth-looking hands stretched out in front of her. \"Yes.\" Liu Rong obediently walked to the Madam. She couldn't help but glance at the Madam from the corner of her eye, and saw the Madam looking at her with a very strange look. At the end, she showed a satisfied smile. \"Grandma really didn't lie to me. Sister Rong's appearance is indeed somewhat similar to that of Ninth Sister. It's just a pity that she is a little thinner. If her expression was a little similar,", "title_en": "Chapter 3"}